title: 'Decided: "the user" is every owned skgrepo together.'
pid: 8b1b1321-76b0-4bfb-9f5d-d0af4de9897d
body: |2-
  Exactly as under an owned root: an overrider counts as the user's if
  its home skgrepo is owned, whichever owned skgrepo that is. Override
  monogamy is already checked across all owned data, so the owned
  overriders of a node form one chain, and following "the most private
  shown skgrepo" or one chosen skgrepo would only show less of it. The
  skgrepo restriction still hides what it hides.
